  'A 22-year-old university student presents with a 14-month history of repeated intrusive thoughts that she will contaminate her family with germs, which she recognises as excessive and irrational but cannot suppress. She washes her hands over 40 times a day until they are raw and cracked, and this now takes up more than 3 hours daily, causing her to miss lectures. She denies low mood or psychotic symptoms.',
  'What is the most appropriate first-line management?',
  array['OCD','obsessive-compulsive disorder','CBT with ERP']
),
('e3000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000004', 'ukmla', '8d54a4e2-b8b2-4f45-a133-a7652815561e',
  'draft', 'core',
  'A 40-year-old firefighter presents 5 weeks after attending a building collapse in which two colleagues died. He reports recurrent distressing nightmares and intrusive flashbacks of the event, avoidance of the fire station, exaggerated startle response, and irritability. He has stopped sleeping properly and has taken time off work. He has no prior psychiatric history.',
  'What is the most appropriate first-line treatment?',
  array['PTSD','trauma-focused CBT','post-traumatic stress disorder']
),
('e3000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000005', 'ukmla', '8d54a4e2-b8b2-4f45-a133-a7652815561e',
  'draft', 'core',
  'A 46-year-old man attends his GP for the sixth time in 3 months, convinced he has bowel cancer despite a normal colonoscopy, normal FIT test, and normal bloods 6 weeks ago. He constantly checks his body for lumps, researches symptoms online for hours daily, and is not reassured by previous normal results. He has no change in bowel habit, weight loss, or PR bleeding. He denies low mood.',
  'What is the most likely diagnosis?',
  array['health anxiety','illness anxiety disorder']
),
