  'draft', 'foundation',
  'A 72-year-old man with a large right middle cerebral artery ischaemic stroke and expressive dysphasia requires an urgent CT-confirmed decompressive procedure discussion. He is unable to understand the explanation of the risks and benefits despite simplified language, visual aids, and time, and cannot retain or weigh this information to communicate a decision. He has no advance decision or lasting power of attorney for health and welfare.',
