  'draft', 'core',
  'A 35-year-old man with an established diagnosis of paranoid schizophrenia is brought to the emergency department by his family, who report he has stopped his antipsychotic medication 3 weeks ago and now believes his food is being poisoned by the government. He refuses admission and wants to leave. On assessment, he is calm but clearly deluded, has poor insight, and there are concerns about his ability to look after himself safely at home; there is no current medical need for hospital assessment beyond his mental state.',
