  'draft', 'core',
  'A 44-year-old woman with a long-standing diagnosis of bipolar affective disorder was admitted 3 weeks ago under Section 2 of the Mental Health Act with a manic relapse. The diagnosis and treatment plan are now clear, but she continues to lack insight, refuses medication, and remains at significant risk if discharged. The responsible clinician believes ongoing compulsory treatment in hospital is required beyond the current 28-day period.',
